# Ode to Joy, the theme only (repertoire plan: ode-to-joy-theme). Beethoven's tune from the
# finale of the Ninth Symphony, in G on strings 3 and 2 in first position: 16 bars in A A B A
# form. The first A ends on A (it waits), the second and the last on G (home). The B phrase has
# two quick eighth-note pairs (B-C) and ends on the low D, the open string 4.
# Fingers: A = string 3 fret 2 (finger 2), C = string 2 fret 1 (finger 1), D = string 2 fret 3
# (finger 3). The teacher strums G and D, changing where the tune needs it.
title: Ode to Joy (theme)
id: ode-to-joy-theme
composer: Ludwig van Beethoven
source: Theme of the finale of Symphony No. 9 (1824, published 1826); new arrangement for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Beethoven died in 1827); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 2
tags: melody, classical, stepwise, dotted rhythm
tempo: 96
time: 4/4
key: G

track: Melody
role: lead
